      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That concern about localized economic vacuum is a major challenge, as the geographical skills required for green jobs often do not match those in legacy energy industries. Without robust, targeted transition programs, regions reliant on coal and oil face severe structural unemployment and potential economic contraction. Policymakers would need substantial investment in regional retraining and infrastructure to mitigate this risk and prevent concentrated recession.",
      "source": "target",
